      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so you're basically suggesting we use those \"traditional\" or \"cultural\" aesthetics to make these specific markets feel more comfortable, while for the others (like Japan or Ireland), we stick to more standard, \"modern\" minimalist or clean looks? \n\nit feels a bit like we're categorizing users into \"modern/global\" vs \"traditional/local.\" specifically for the Nigerian and UAE profiles, are you suggesting that to get high conversion, we should lean into those ethnic-coded visual cues because they might not associate a \"minimalist/white\" Western-style UI with a high-end or professional financial service? like, is there a risk that if we go too \"clean and white\" for those markets, they won't take the app seriously?",
      "source": "evaluator"
